# Shopify Skeleton Theme — Project Overview

## What this is

A minimalist, Theme-Store-ready Shopify theme with a TypeScript + Vite build pipeline. Intentionally small and foundational — not a fully-featured theme.

## Architecture

```
layout/            # theme.liquid (main), password.liquid
sections/          # Liquid sections with {% schema %} — core UI units
snippets/          # Reusable Liquid partials
blocks/            # Nestable theme blocks (group.liquid, text.liquid, …)
templates/         # JSON templates (index, product, collection, cart, blog, …)
config/            # settings_schema.json + settings_data.json
locales/           # Merchant strings + en.default.schema.json (schema t: keys)
assets/            # Static files + Vite output (theme.js, theme.css, critical.css)
src/scripts/       # TS → bundled entry theme.ts → assets/theme.js (+ lazy chunks)
src/scripts/sections/  # Optional: registerXxx + lazy *.runtime.ts for heavy sections
src/styles/        # SCSS → assets/theme.css via theme.scss
src/types/         # TypeScript declarations (shopify.d.ts)
docs/              # Internal dev docs (registry, color system, section principles)
```

## Naming & file placement

| Kind | Filename pattern | Notes |
|------|------------------|--------|
| Reusable marketing / layout section | `section-<feature>.liquid` | e.g. `section-hero-slider`, `section-feature-grid` |
| Template-bound section (needs `product`, `collection`, …) | `main-<context>.liquid` | e.g. `main-product`, `main-collection` |
| Global / chrome | `header`, `footer`, `cart-drawer`, section groups | As needed in `layout/` |
| Snippet | `kebab-case.liquid` | Prefix groups: `pdp-*`, `header-*`, `article-*`, etc. |
| Section SCSS | `src/styles/sections/_section-<feature>.scss` or `_main-<context>.scss` | `@forward` from `sections/index.scss` |
| Section TS (simple) | `src/scripts/<name>.ts` | `registerSection` + init/destroy at repo root |
| Section TS (heavy bundle) | `src/scripts/sections/<name>.ts` + `*.runtime.ts` | Thin register file; dynamic `import()` of runtime (see hero slider) |

Internal references: `docs/SECTION_ARCHITECTURE_DESIGN_PRINCIPLES.md` (one job per section), `docs/SECTION_REGISTRY.md` (data-section-type, boot, editor).

## Build system

- **Vite** (`vite.config.ts`): entry `src/scripts/theme.ts` → `assets/theme.js` (ES module + code-split chunks in `assets/`, see `chunkFileNames`). One bundled `theme.css` (`cssCodeSplit: false`).
- SCSS compiled through Vite; `loadPaths: ['src/styles']` enables bare `@use` imports
- `emptyOutDir: false` — Vite writes to `assets/` without deleting other files
- `npm run dev` = `concurrently "shopify theme dev" "vite build --watch"`
- `npm run build` = production Vite build

## Key dependencies

- **gsap** — all JS animations (drawer slide, submenu reveal, hero transitions)
- **swiper** — carousels/sliders (hero, product gallery thumbs)
- **@shopify/cli** — theme dev server, theme check, packaging

## Code formatting

- Prettier: no semicolons, single quotes, 2-space indent, trailing commas (es5)
- ESLint: `@typescript-eslint/recommended`, `no-explicit-any: warn`
- TypeScript: strict mode, ES2020 target, bundler module resolution

## Section registration pattern

Every **interactive** section follows this flow:
1. Define `registerXxxSection()` in `src/scripts/xxx.ts` or `src/scripts/sections/xxx.ts`
2. Call `registerSection(SECTION_TYPE, init, destroy)` from `section-registry.ts`
3. Import and call `registerXxxSection()` in `theme.ts` **before** `bootSections()`
4. Liquid root uses `data-section-type` (exact string match) and `data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"`
5. `bootSections()` runs after registrations; MutationObserver + `shopify:section:load/unload` handled by registry

Sections with **no JS**: omit `data-section-type`; no TS registration; still add schema + styles as needed.

## Liquid conventions

- Sections expose settings via `{% schema %}` JSON
- **Section shell:** page-style sections should use `{% render 'section-styles', section: section %}` + class `shopify-section-wrapper` on the root when merchants need shared padding, margin, background, and border controls (see `snippets/section-styles.liquid`, `_section-wrapper.scss`). Skip for overlays, drawer/modal sections, or layout that conflicts (agent decides). Details: `.cursor/rules/liquid-patterns.mdc` → *Section shell*.
- **Typography scale:** merchant-controlled type sizes are Global CSS variables from `snippets/css-variables.liquid` (`--font-size-xs` … `--font-size-4xl`, line-height tokens). Use `var(--font-size-*, <fallback>)` in SCSS and `{% stylesheet %}` so **Base font size** in theme settings applies. Details: `.cursor/rules/scss-styles.mdc` → *Typography and font size*.
- CSS variables on section root for dynamic settings: `style="--gap: {{ block.settings.gap }}px"`
- Prefer `{% stylesheet %}` / `{% javascript %}` for co-located section CSS/JS
- Critical CSS in `assets/critical.css`; non-critical via Vite (`assets/theme.css`)
- Font loading via `snippets/font-pairing-loader.liquid` in `<head>`
- Cart routes set in `layout/theme.liquid` as `window.__themeRoutes` (preferred over `Shopify.routes`)

## When editing this project

- Always check `data-section-type` matches between Liquid and TypeScript
- Run `npm run check` (Theme Check) after Liquid changes
- Run `npm run build` after TypeScript/SCSS changes to verify compilation
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` in all JS animations
- **JS-driven sections:** carousels/sliders and similar should use **loading → reveal** after load/init and an optional merchant **toggle** for **scroll-into-view** animation. See `.cursor/rules/liquid-patterns.mdc` → *JS-driven UI* and `src/scripts/**/*.ts` runtime patterns.
- Use AbortController for section cleanup in `destroy()` functions
